  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVATION OF SEA TURTLES IN COTE D&apos;IVOIRE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO IMPLEMENT A SEA TURTLE CONSERVATION PROJECT IN IVORY COAST. IVORY COAST HOSTS IMPORTANT OLIVE RIDLEY, GREEN AND LEATHERBACK NESTING AND IMPORTANT FORAGING GROUNDS FOR SEVERAL SEA TURTLE SPECIES. THE INTENT OF THIS PROJECT IS TO ADDRESS THREATS TO SEA TURTLES FROM POACHING AND FISHERIES BYCATCH MORTALITY. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: 1) CONDUCTING COMMUNITY BASED NIGHT PATROLS ALONG THE 30 KM ROC-MANI-KABLAKE BEACH AND THE 8 KM ASSEOUFOUE BEACH THROUGHOUT THE MARINE TURTLE NESTING SEASON TO PREVENT POACHING OF NESTS AND NESTING FEMALES, 2) RELOCATING NESTS THREATENED BY TIDES TO SAFE BEACH HATCHERIES, AND 3) WORKING WITH FISHERMAN TO SAFELY RELEASE TURTLES CAUGHT IN GILL NETS IN GRAND BEREBY AREA.</narrative>
  </description>
